  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode:00CBFDW968000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "title": "Aperas-artifact-projection-design.md",
    "text": "`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A names three projection modes that turn a stored `BlockNode` tree back into an output: Artifact Projection (serialize back to the physical `.md` file, always fully unfolded regardless of each block's `unfolded` state), the Human UI, and the Agentic BFS interface. This doc settles the design for the first of the three — Artifact Projection, the direct inverse of `astParser.ts`'s Markdown → tree transform. The other two modes are out of scope here. The design below is settled; nothing has been implemented yet.",
    "parent": "FolderNode:00CBFDYW1R002",
    "type": "root",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CBFDZ5GG001"
    ],
    "path": "archive/tdb-era/Aperas-artifact-projection-design.md",
    "fileHash": "17fc83bc70d013c020b5e1e69c979a124ed99b457caf5f710dcb7bbae9ddda0c",
    "lastTrackedAt": "2026-09-07T08:38:56.921Z",
    "ingestedHash": "17fc83bc70d013c020b5e1e69c979a124ed99b457caf5f710dcb7bbae9ddda0c",
    "lastIngestedAt": "2026-09-07T08:39:08.738Z"
  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode:00CBFDW96G000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "title": "Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md",
    "text": "The original roadmap (`Aperas-design.md`'s Development Roadmap) only ever named one assertion- related deliverable — Phase 2's \"graph search skill\" — and treated the Human UI (Phase 1) as the thing that lets humans/agents see what's in the graph at all. Neither assumption survived Phase 0 finishing:",
